\fs18\fsmilli9240 The Egyptians recognized five planets and called them the "stars that knew no rest" or (more ancient way) "eyes of [god] Horus"\
". Their movement across\
the heavens reminded the Egyptians of five gods sailing across the sky in their solar barque (boat).\
The planet now known as Jupiter was called "Horus Who Limits the Two Lands"; Mars was "Horus of the Horizon"; Mercury was "Sebegu", associated with Set; Saturn was "Horus the Bull of the Sky"; and Venus was "the God of the Morning[8]\

